      "output": "Water is a chemical substance that is essential for life on Earth. Here is a breakdown of what it is, how it is made, and why it is important:\n\n### 1. Chemical Composition\nChemically, water is known as **dihydrogen monoxide**. Its chemical formula is **$H_2O$**. This means that every molecule of water is made up of:\n*   **Two hydrogen atoms**\n*   **One oxygen atom**\n\nThese atoms are bonded together by a covalent bond.\n\n### 2. Physical States\nWater is unique because it can exist naturally in all three states of matter at standard temperatures and pressures:\n*   **Solid:** Ice (when frozen)\n*   **Liquid:** The form we drink and use for washing\n*   **Gas:** Water vapor (steam)\n\n### 3. Key Properties\nWater has several unique properties that make it vital for life:\n*   **Polarity:** The water molecule is \"bent,\" which gives it a positive end and a negative end. This allows water to stick to itself (cohesion) and to other substances (adhesion).\n*   **Universal Solvent:** Because of its polarity, water can dissolve more substances than any other liquid. This helps transport nutrients and waste in living organisms.\n*   **High Heat Capacity:** Water can absorb a lot of heat without getting hot. This helps regulate the temperature of the Earth and keeps the human body stable.\n*   **Density Anomaly:** Unlike most substances, water is less dense as a solid (ice) than as a liquid. This is why ice floats, which insulates bodies of water and allows life to exist beneath the ice in winter.\n\n### 4. Biological Importance\nWater is the primary component of all living things. It makes up about 60% of the human body and is necessary for:\n*   Digestion and nutrient absorption\n*   Temperature regulation (sweating and panting)\n*   Lubricating joints\n*   Removing waste through urination and sweating"
